{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>O cananeu estava então na terra.</b> Rashi explicou que ele ia conquistando a descendência de Shem, pois a terra coube à porção de Shem quando Noach dividiu a terra entre seus filhos. E é intrigante, pois na parashat shelach lekha Rashi explicou sobre o versículo ״וחברון שבע שנים נבנתה״ que Mitzrayim gave it to his firstborn son, but it was built from everything good, like one of the seven of Tzoan, and so it is concluded in Sotah, chapter ואלו נאמרין — thus it implies that Hebron, which is in the land of Israel, fell to the portion of Ham. One may answer that it is a dispute, for in Torat Kohanim it concludes: for what reason did the Canaanites merit to dwell in their land 47 years more than the Egyptians? How? Seven years that Hebron was built before Tzoan of Egypt, and forty years that Israel dwelt in the wilderness after Egypt was destroyed — because they set aside a portion for Abraham the righteous and said to him: ״נשיא אלהים אתה בתוכנו״."], :book "genesis", :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :pt, :chapter 12, :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:35:30.686382207Z", :translated-from :en, :model "glm-5.2"}